{
  "version": 1,
  "about": [
    "Labelled category pairs for measuring the semantic review.",
    "",
    "SYNTHETIC AND NON-SENSITIVE. Every value here was written for this file. No",
    "participant, no client and no real workbook content appears in it. The two",
    "COLLISION SHAPES it is built around are real — a zero-return band worded two",
    "ways by two questionnaires, and a line of business capitalised two ways — but",
    "the strings are reconstructions, and the surrounding scales are invented.",
    "",
    "HOW TO READ `truth`:",
    "  same      - a person who has read both instruments would group these.",
    "  different - grouping these would be a defect. A merge here is the failure",
    "              the whole feature exists to prevent, and the measurement that",
    "              matters most is that this never happens without a human.",
    "  context   - it depends on the question. The system must not settle it; the",
    "              correct behaviour is to raise it with a warning, or leave it.",
    "",
    "`expectProposal` is what the DETERMINISTIC scan should do. For `different`",
    "pairs it is usually false, but not always: an accent pair that happens to be",
    "two different words is worth ASKING about even though the answer is no. What",
    "is never acceptable is acting on it."
  ],
